From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: hold the SD reader port's DART while the
 reader is off

With pcie_apple.t8132_sd_port_off (on by default) an empty slot takes
the J604's SD reader off the bus, stops its port's link and holds the
endpoint in reset, ten seconds after probe on a boot. Removing the
endpoint drops the last runtime PM reference on the port's DART, and
the DART's runtime suspend, which reads every stream's TCR and TTBRs to
save them, runs later from the PM workqueue. When it lands after the
port is stopped the read ends in a synchronous external abort and an
SError, and with kernel.panic=0 the boot stops until the watchdog
resets the Mac about a minute later.

The panic records of two such resets on the J604 show it. One was an
SError on CPU 2 after a data abort (EC 0x25, DFSC 0x10, a read) at
apple_dart_save_state+0x44, and the FAR was in dart-apcie2
(0x492000000). The other was an SError on CPU 1 with the L2C latching
0x492001000, dart-apcie2's TCR block. The boot crumb of the first one
stopped at 11 s, which is when the reader goes down. Both reset loops
happened on two kernels with this code.

Take a runtime PM reference on the port's DART, found through the
host's iommu-map, before the endpoint is removed. Drop it after the
reader is back and rescanned, when its own streams hold the DART
again, or when the port goes away. The DART then saves nothing while
its port is down. Its power domain stays on either way, with the
radio's DART in it.

Fixes: d5e1fa8bab00 ("PCI: apple: power a card reader port down while its slot is empty")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index fd2c27ca03..1f92eaebc1 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -635,6 +635,7 @@ struct apple_pcie_port {
 	struct list_head	sd_entry;
 	bool			sd_off;		/* powered down for an empty slot */
 	struct pci_dev		*sd_rp_held;	/* its root port, kept active while it is down */
+	struct device		*sd_dart;	/* its DART, kept active while it is down */
 };
 
 static bool apple_radio_writer_closed(struct apple_pcie *pcie);
@@ -2999,6 +3000,37 @@ static int apple_pcie_port_reset_endpoint(struct apple_pcie *pcie,
 #define APPLE_PCIE_SD_DEBOUNCE_MS	200
 #define APPLE_PCIE_SD_BOOT_DELAY_MS	10000
 
+/*
+ * Once the port is stopped and its endpoint held in reset, a read of the port's DART registers
+ * can end in a synchronous external abort and an SError: on the J604 the boot stopped there,
+ * with dart-apcie2's TCR read from apple_dart_save_state(). Removing the endpoint drops the
+ * DART's last runtime PM reference, and its runtime suspend, which saves those registers, runs
+ * later from the PM workqueue, so it can land after the port is stopped. Hold the DART active
+ * from before the endpoint goes until the reader is back: nothing reads it while it is down.
+ */
+static void apple_pcie_sd_hold_dart(struct apple_pcie *pcie, struct apple_pcie_port *port,
+				    struct pci_dev *rp)
+{
+	struct of_phandle_args args = {};
+	struct platform_device *pdev;
+
+	if (port->sd_dart || !rp || !rp->subordinate)
+		return;
+	if (of_map_iommu_id(pcie->dev->of_node, PCI_DEVID(rp->subordinate->number, 0), &args) ||
+	    !args.np)
+		return;
+	pdev = of_find_device_by_node(args.np);
+	of_node_put(args.np);
+	if (!pdev)
+		return;
+	if (pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev) < 0) {
+		put_device(&pdev->dev);
+		dev_warn(pcie->dev, "port %pOF: could not hold its DART\n", port->np);
+		return;
+	}
+	port->sd_dart = &pdev->dev;
+}
+
 static void apple_pcie_sd_power_down(struct apple_pcie *pcie, struct apple_pcie_port *port)
 {
 	struct pci_host_bridge *bridge = pci_host_bridge_from_priv(pcie);
@@ -3017,6 +3049,7 @@ static void apple_pcie_sd_power_down(struct apple_pcie *pcie, struct apple_pcie_
 	/* The port's reset takes the root port's config too: kept for the power-up. */
 	if (port->sd_rp_held)
 		pci_save_state(port->sd_rp_held);
+	apple_pcie_sd_hold_dart(pcie, port, rp);
 	if (rp && rp->subordinate)
 		list_for_each_entry_safe_reverse(dev, tmp, &rp->subordinate->devices, bus_list)
 			pci_stop_and_remove_bus_device(dev);
@@ -3040,7 +3073,14 @@ static void apple_pcie_sd_power_down(struct apple_pcie *pcie, struct apple_pcie_
 static void apple_pcie_sd_release_rp(struct apple_pcie_port *port)
 {
 	struct pci_dev *rp = port->sd_rp_held;
+	struct device *dart = port->sd_dart;
 
+	/* After the rescan: the reader's own streams hold the DART again. */
+	port->sd_dart = NULL;
+	if (dart) {
+		pm_runtime_put(dart);
+		put_device(dart);
+	}
 	if (!rp)
 		return;
 	port->sd_rp_held = NULL;
-- 
